The highest GDPR tier is fines of up to 20 000 000 EUR. For an undertaking, it is up to 4 % of total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher [cite:B:gdpr-2016:438].

This tier covers infringements of:
- the basic processing principles, including consent conditions (Articles 5, 6, 7 and 9);
- data subjects' rights (Articles 12 to 22);
- transfers to third countries or international organisations (Articles 44 to 49);
- obligations under Member State law adopted under Chapter IX;
- non-compliance with a supervisory authority's order or limitation on processing [cite:B:gdpr-2016:438].

Non-compliance with a supervisory authority order under Article 58(2) also falls in this tier [cite:B:gdpr-2016:439].

The lower tier is up to 10 000 000 EUR or 2 % [cite:B:gdpr-2016:437].

